messages:
alex: Heads-up — we're getting reports from Expo users that our JS SDK breaks on build: runtime errors about 'crypto' and 'ReadableStream'. Anyone seen this?

tara: Yep saw one in Sentry earlier. expo-managed apps don't have node crypto or stream/web. Error stack points to https://unpkg.com/redwood-sdk/dist/index.js line ~200.

josh: Is this the ESM build only? I thought we had a CJS fallback.

alex: The package publishes both, but the bundle's runtime assumptions differ. The ESM entry imports 'stream/web' and uses globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues. On RN those are undefined.

nina: Short-term workaround for customers: add polyfills in metro config or import 'react-native-get-random-values' and 'stream-browser-polyfill'. But that's gross for onboarding.

alex: Example from a user: 
```
TypeError: crypto.getRandomValues is not a function
    at secureRandom (node_modules/redwood-sdk/dist/index.js:198:24)
```

tara: For Expo specifically recommend expo-random or react-native-get-random-values + global.crypto = { getRandomValues: ... } in app entry. But we need better DX.

josh: Agreed. We should consider adding a react-native-specific entrypoint in package.json and conditional exports. That way bundlers pick RN-safe build automatically.

nina: Yup. Proposed package.json exports map (sketch):
```
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.cjs",
    "react-native": "./dist/rn/index.js",
    "worker": "./dist/edge/index.mjs"
  }
}
```
This lets Metro pick "react-native" field.

alex: Nice. For edge/deno we also need a build that avoids Node-only globals and uses Web Streams + fetch. Current edge build expects ReadableStream but RN (JSC) doesn't have it.

tara: Another problem: typings. Types reference Node types (Buffer, ReadableStream from lib.dom) which clash with TS projects targeting react-native. Users get type errors. We should ship a separate .d.ts for RN/edge or use conditional types in package exports ("types":...).

josh: Quick checklist for a dev-ex release: 
- add react-native build that uses expo-compatible crypto and no stream/web imports
- add conditional exports including "react-native" and "worker"
- provide a tiny RN polyfill snippet in README + example app in /examples/expo
- fix types to avoid Node-only references

nina: I'll draft a minimal polyfill snippet for README: 
```
// App.js (very early)
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
if (typeof globalThis.crypto === 'undefined') {
  globalThis.crypto = {
    getRandomValues: global.getRandomValues || (arr => { throw new Error('no RNG'); })
  };
}
// polyfill for ReadableStream fallback
if (typeof globalThis.ReadableStream === 'undefined') {
  // fall back to using response.body from fetch when possible
  // or include a tiny ponyfill: install 'web-streams-polyfill'
}
```

alex: We should also add an expo example in monorepo that just does quick text generation. Onboarding friction is mostly "what to install and where to init".

tara: One more edge-compat note: abort controller support. Edge runtimes use web AbortController, RN may not. Make sure SDK accepts signal: any and normalizes.

josh: I'll open a PR to add the RN build + exports mapping and an examples/expo minimal app. Will also include tests that run the RN bundle through metro-bundler to catch obvious Kryptonite.

nina: Can we add a small diagnostic helper that logs missing globals at runtime and gives actionable steps? Something like: 
```
if (!globalThis.crypto || !globalThis.ReadableStream) {
  console.warn('[redwood-sdk] Missing runtime globals: crypto=%s ReadableStream=%s — see https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk#react-native', !!globalThis.crypto, !!globalThis.ReadableStream)
}
```

alex: Love it. Tara — can you own the README bits + example content? Josh do the packaging/exports work, Nina do the diagnostic + polyfill notes. I'll coordinate QA with a couple Expo users.

tara: Yep. Will add a short troubleshooting section and a one-file expo example with minimal dependencies.

josh: PR to come in a few hours. tagging @devex-bot to create a tracking ticket.

devex-bot: Created task DEVEX-5123: "React Native/Expo: RN-specific build + polyfills + examples" — assigned to josh, tara, nina. ETA 1 week. :white_check_mark:

alex: Thanks everyone. Let's keep the changes small and ship quickly — high impact for onboarding. :rocket:
